### Introduction
The UnityRuntimePlugins package is a Unity 6 package that provides a framework for creating plugins for the Unity 6 editor and runtime.  
It provides a simple interface for creating plugins and provides a framework for sharing data between plugins and the main application. Plugins are loaded at runtime from a specified directory or its sub-directories. Plugins are deployed and loaded as zip files containing a directory tree of plugin modules. It can be imported into a Unity project via the Package Manager in order to create new plugins.    

Each plugin module is organized as a sub-directory of the plugin. The sub-directory contains a `manifest.json` file that defines the plugin module, as well as the plugin code and assets. Each module can contain a client folder, a server folder, or both. It may also contain a common folder for code and assets that are used by both client and server. 

Assets in each of the folders are organized into subdirectories that contain assets loaded by the Addressables system or streaming assets. When a plugin is loaded, the plugin manager will load the assets for the appropriate runtime (client or server) as well as the common assets. A module also has a `source_code~` directory that contains source code which is compiled to WASM when the plugin is built. Source code is not used at runtime, only the compiled WASM modules placed in the streaming assets directory by the build process.

